module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.AffineOverBase
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor.PsiPullbackLeg

/-!
# Lemma 01O1's `θ`-assertion at the tag's own second leg

Every form of [Stacks, Tag 01O1]'s `θ`-assertion in this repository takes the second leg of the
characterising triangle as an **arbitrary** degreewise family `v_n : f^*𝒜_{nd} ⟶ r^*𝒪(nd)`:
`...RelativeVeroneseTwists.existsUnique_theta_of_degreeOpen`,
`existsUnique_theta_of_degreeOpen_of_nonneg` and
`existsUnique_theta_of_degreeOpen_of_nonneg_situation` all quantify over `v`. That is a
generalisation, and a safe one, but it leaves the tag's own leg unnamed: the tag's `v` is the
homogeneous-section map `ψ` of [Stacks, Tag 01NR], and nothing said that the conclusion applies
to *it*.

`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.TwistData.psiLegVeronese` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor.PsiPullbackLeg` is that leg — `ψ` transposed across
the adjunction `π^* ⊣ π_*` and base-changed along `r` — and this file instantiates the
`θ`-assertion at it.

## Main results

* `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.existsUnique_theta_psiLeg`: **the
  `θ`-assertion at the tag's own source and the tag's own second leg.** Everything the statement
  still asks of its caller is the single hypothesis `hv`, the commutativity of the triangle for
  `psiLegVeronese` in nonnegative degrees **for some** degree-one datum `α`.

Every other input of that statement is already available. Over an arbitrary base
`...RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.thetaMorphism` produces the morphism `r`, its landing in the
degree-`d` locus and the over-`S` identity `r ≫ π = f` that `psiLegVeronese` needs in order to
exist at all; over an affine base
`...RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.exists_hom_overBase_degreeOne_datum_of_isAffine` produces those
three together with a degree-one datum.

## The one hypothesis that remains, and why `α` is quantified inside it

`hv` reads: for some `α : r^*𝒪(d) ≅ ℒ` and every `n ≥ 0`,

`(ψ-leg)_n ≫ (laurentComparisonOfDegreeOpen … α)_n = P.twisting.app n` :

the twist datum's own homogeneous-section map, pulled back and followed by the recognition
isomorphism, is the quadruple's own `ψ`.

**`α` is quantified inside `hv`, not alongside it.** It used to be a binder of its own,
independent of the quadruple `P`. That was mis-stated. By
`...GradedLaurentRecognition.pieceIso_one_comp_oneIsoL` the degree-one component of the
recognition isomorphism is `α` itself read through `ℒ^{⊗ 1} ≅ ℒ`, so the degree-one instance of
the equation is `ψ_univ|_{degree 1} ≫ α = ψ|_{degree 1}`: it *selects* `α` against `P`'s own `ψ`,
and a statement taking the two as independent arguments said nothing about the `α` a caller would
actually hold. That reading is
`...RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.degreeOne_triangle_iff`. Quantifying `α` inside the hypothesis
leaves the conclusion untouched and makes the hypothesis weaker — a caller holding `α` and the old
equation holds the pair — so the statement below is strictly stronger than the one it replaces.

Three things about the remaining equation are worth recording, because they rule out the cheap
routes.

**It is not a definition in disguise.** Setting `v_n := P.twisting.app n ≫ (comparison)⁻¹_n` would
make `hv` hold by construction and the conclusion vacuous. `psiLegVeronese` is built from the
field `TwistData.ψ` and the adjunction alone, and mentions neither the quadruple nor the
comparison, so the equation above has content.

**It does not reduce to degree one.** `v ≫ θ` and `P.twisting` are both degreewise families out
of `f^*𝒜^{(d)}`, and two such families agreeing in degree one agree everywhere only when `𝒜` is
generated by `𝒜_d` over `𝒜_0`. Without that, the degree-one instance of `hv` is strictly weaker
than `hv`.

**The induction it would go by is not available.**
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedLaurentRecognition.pieceIso`, the degreewise component of the
comparison, is defined by recursion on the degree, so `hv` would be proved by induction, and the
step needs the second leg to be multiplicative: `v_i ⊗ v_j` followed by the multiplication of the
target equal to the multiplication of the source followed by `v_{i+j}`. The quadruple's side of
that is available — it is the field `RelativeProjQcohSheaf.Twisting.app_mul`, an equation between
composites of morphisms of sheaves of modules.

The twist datum's side is available for the leg *before* its base change along `r`:
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor.PsiLegMultiplicative` instantiates the `HEq` field
`TwistData.ψ_mul` as a square of sheaf morphisms, giving
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists.TwistData.psiTranspose_mulSheaf` and the homomorphism
of graded algebras `TwistData.psiTransposeHom`.

The transport of that multiplicativity along `r` and into the `d`-divisible grading — the same
statement for `TwistData.psiLegVeronese`, which is the family `hv` is about — is now available
too: `StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.TwistTensor.PsiLegVeroneseMultiplicative` proves it as
`TwistData.psiLegVeronese_mulSheaf` and assembles the homomorphism of graded algebras
`TwistData.psiLegVeroneseHom`.

**So both multiplicativities are available, and the induction still does not close.** With them,
the degree-`n` instance of the equation gives

`mulSheaf (f^*𝒜^{(d)}) n 1 ≫ ((ψ-leg)_{n+1} ≫ comparison_{n+1}) =`
  `mulSheaf (f^*𝒜^{(d)}) n 1 ≫ ψ_{n+1}` ,

and cancelling the multiplication needs it to be an **epimorphism** — that is, needs `𝒜_{(n+1)d}`
to be generated by `𝒜_{nd} · 𝒜_d`, which is degree-one generation of `𝒜^{(d)}` over `𝒜_0`. That
is not among Tag 01O1's hypotheses, and without it two homomorphisms of graded algebras out of
`f^*𝒜^{(d)}` agreeing in degree one need not agree in degree two. The induction is therefore not
merely unwritten: on the tag's own hypotheses it cannot be made to work, and the equation has to
come from the universal property instead. The sibling module `ThetaTriangle` of this directory
records which single theorem about the universal element of `F_d` on `U_d` it is equivalent to.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01O1](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01O1)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01NU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01NU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits
open Stacks.RingedSpace
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProj
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjBridge
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjQcohSheaf
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwists
open Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeVeroneseTwists

universe u

namespace Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwistChartBridge

variable {S T : Scheme.{u}} {A : SheafGradedAlgebra.{u} S} {d : ℕ} {f : T ⟶ S}

/-! ### The `θ`-assertion at the tag's own second leg -/

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01O1.** *The comparison `θ`, the commutativity of its characterising
triangle and its uniqueness, with the second leg of the triangle being the tag's own.*

This is `...RelativeVeroneseTwists.existsUnique_theta_of_degreeOpen_of_nonneg_situation` with the
arbitrary degreewise family `v` replaced by
`...RelativeProjTwists.TwistData.psiLegVeronese`, the homogeneous-section map of [Stacks, Tag
01NR] transposed across `π^* ⊣ π_*` and base-changed along `r`. The over-`S` identity `hr` is
what lets that leg exist; over an arbitrary base
`...RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.thetaMorphism` supplies `r`, `hg` and `hr`, and over an affine
base `...RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.exists_hom_overBase_degreeOne_datum_of_isAffine` supplies
those three together with a degree-one datum.

The hypothesis `hv` is the same triangle as in the statement it specialises, now for one named
family instead of all of them, **and with the degree-one datum `α` quantified inside it rather
than taken as an independent binder**: the degree-one instance of the triangle determines `α`
against `P`'s own `ψ` (`...RelativeProjTwistChartBridge.degreeOne_triangle_iff`), so a statement
that took the two as unrelated arguments was mis-stated. Moving `α` inside leaves the conclusion
untouched and weakens the hypothesis, so this is strictly stronger than the earlier form. See the
module docstring for why `hv` is neither a definition in disguise, nor reducible to its degree-one
instance, nor reachable by an induction on the degree. -/
theorem existsUnique_theta_psiLeg (D : TwistData A) (hd : 0 < d)
    (r : T ⟶ (relativeProj A).scheme)
    (hg : ∀ t : T, r.base t ∈ (relativeProj A).degreeOpen d)
    (hr : r ≫ (relativeProj A).toBase = f)
    (P : Quadruple f (situationAlgebra A) (d : ℤ))
    (hv : ∃ α : (pullbackTwistVeronese D (d : ℤ) r).piece 1 ≅ P.L,
      ∀ n : ℕ, D.psiLegVeronese r hr (d : ℤ) (n : ℤ) ≫
        (laurentComparisonOfDegreeOpen D d r hg α).hom.app (n : ℤ) = P.twisting.app (n : ℤ)) :
    ∃ θ' : pullbackTwistVeronese D (d : ℤ) r ≅ laurent P.L,
      (∀ n : ℤ, D.psiLegVeronese r hr (d : ℤ) n ≫ θ'.hom.app n = P.twisting.app n) ∧
        ∃! Θ : pullbackTwistVeronese D (d : ℤ) r ⟶ laurent P.L,
          ∀ n : ℤ, D.psiLegVeronese r hr (d : ℤ) n ≫ Θ.app n = P.twisting.app n :=
  existsUnique_theta_of_degreeOpen_of_nonneg_situation D d r hg P
    (Int.natCast_pos.mpr hd) (D.psiLegVeronese r hr (d : ℤ)) hv.choose hv.choose_spec

end Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.RelativeProjTwistChartBridge

end
